IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc29-xxviii-0-peace-810`

-- ccc29-tests-xxviii-0-peace-810.l4 -- tests for sections 810, 810.01 and 810.011 of the Criminal Code (Canada).
-- Every expected value is written from the text before the run, beside its assertion. Argument order is the GIVEN order of each function.

§ `Tests -- section 810`

-- 810(1): who may lay an information: (fears on reasonable grounds, the feared event).
#ASSERT `s 810(1) an information may be laid before a justice` TRUE `s 810(1)(a) personal injury to the person or to their intimate partner or child, or damage to their property` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(1) an information may be laid before a justice` TRUE `s 810(1)(b) an offence under section 162.1` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(1) an information may be laid before a justice` TRUE `s 810(1) another feared event` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810(1) an information may be laid before a justice` FALSE `s 810(1)(a) personal injury to the person or to their intimate partner or child, or damage to their property` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810(2): the justice who receives the information shall cause the parties to appear.
#ASSERT `s 810(2) the justice is required to cause the parties to appear` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(2) the justice is required to cause the parties to appear` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810(3): the order of a recognizance: "If ... satisfied"; period not more than 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 810(3) the justice or court may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3) the justice or court may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810(3) the period of the recognizance is not more than 12 months` 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3) the period of the recognizance is not more than 12 months` 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 810(3.01): commitment if the defendant fails or refuses; term not more than 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 810(3.01) the justice or court may commit the defendant to prison` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.01) the justice or court may commit the defendant to prison` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810(3.01) the term of imprisonment is not more than 12 months` 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.01) the term of imprisonment is not more than 12 months` 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 810(3.02): the conditions: (the condition, reasonable, considered desirable).
#ASSERT `s 810(3.02) the justice or court may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810(3.02)(a) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.02) the justice or court may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810(3.02)(b) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.02) the justice or court may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810(3.02)(c) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.02) the justice or court may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810(3.02) another reasonable condition` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.02) the justice or court may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810(3.02) another reasonable condition` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810(3.02) the justice or court may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810(3.02) another reasonable condition` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810(3.1): before making an order under (3), consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable; if it is so desirable, add it.
#ASSERT `s 810(3.1) the justice or court is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.1) the justice or court is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.1) the justice or court is required to add the firearms condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.1) the justice or court is required to add the firearms condition` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 810(3.11): where a firearms condition is added, specify the manner and method of surrender: (condition added, the matter).
#ASSERT `s 810(3.11) the justice or court is required to specify in the order the manner and method` TRUE `s 810(3.11)(a) how the things possessed are to be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.11) the justice or court is required to specify in the order the manner and method` TRUE `s 810(3.11)(b) how the authorizations, licences and registration certificates are to be surrendered` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.11) the justice or court is required to specify in the order the manner and method` TRUE `s 810(3.11) another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810(3.11) the justice or court is required to specify in the order the manner and method` FALSE `s 810(3.11)(a) how the things possessed are to be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 810(3.12): where no firearms condition is added, a statement of reasons.
#ASSERT `s 810(3.12) the justice or court is required to include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.12) the justice or court is required to include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 810(3.2): before making the order, consider whether to add either or both of the supplementary conditions: (about to make an order, the condition).
#ASSERT `s 810(3.2) the justice or court is required to consider whether it is desirable to add the condition` TRUE `s 810(3.2)(a) a condition prohibiting the defendant from being at, or within a specified distance of, a place where the person is regularly found` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.2) the justice or court is required to consider whether it is desirable to add the condition` TRUE `s 810(3.2)(b) a condition prohibiting the defendant from communicating with the person, in whole or in part, directly or indirectly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(3.2) the justice or court is required to consider whether it is desirable to add the condition` TRUE `s 810(3.2) another condition` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810(3.2) the justice or court is required to consider whether it is desirable to add the condition` FALSE `s 810(3.2)(a) a condition prohibiting the defendant from being at, or within a specified distance of, a place where the person is regularly found` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 810(4), (4.1), (5).
#ASSERT `s 810(4) the warrant of committal may be in Form 23` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(4) the warrant of committal may be in Form 23` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810(4.1) the justice or court may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(4.1) the justice or court may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(4.1) the justice or court may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810(5) the provisions of this Part apply to the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810(5) the provisions of this Part apply to the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 810.01`

#ASSERT `s 810.01(1) the person may lay an information before a provincial court judge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(1) the person may lay an information before a provincial court judge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.01(1) the person may lay an information before a provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.01(2) the provincial court judge may cause the parties to appear` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(2) the provincial court judge may cause the parties to appear` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.01(3) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(3) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.01(3) the period of the recognizance is not more than 12 months` 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(3) the period of the recognizance is not more than 12 months` 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(3.1) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a longer period` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(3.1) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a longer period` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.01(3.1) the longer period of the recognizance is not more than two years` 24 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(3.1) the longer period of the recognizance is not more than two years` 25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4) the provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4) the provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4) the term of imprisonment does not exceed twelve months` 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4) the term of imprisonment does not exceed twelve months` 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 810.01(4.1): (the condition, reasonable, considered desirable, the Attorney General makes the request).
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.01(4.1)(a) to participate in a treatment program` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.01(4.1)(b) to wear an electronic monitoring device` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.01(4.1)(b) to wear an electronic monitoring device` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.01(4.1)(c) to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the judge` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.01(4.1)(d) to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.01(4.1)(e) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.01(4.1)(f) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.01(4.1)(g) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.01(4.1) another reasonable condition` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.01(4.1) another reasonable condition` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.01(5) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(5) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.01(5) the provincial court judge is required to add the firearms condition and specify the period during which it applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(5) the provincial court judge is required to add the firearms condition and specify the period during which it applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(5.1) the provincial court judge is required to specify in the recognizance how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(5.1) the provincial court judge is required to specify in the recognizance how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(5.2) the provincial court judge is required to include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(5.2) the provincial court judge is required to include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(6) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(6) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(6) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(6) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(7) subsections 810(4) and (5) apply to the recognizance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(7) subsections 810(4) and (5) apply to the recognizance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.01(8) Attorney General` TRUE `s 810.01(8) the Attorney General of Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(8) Attorney General` TRUE `s 810.01(8) the Attorney General of the province in which the proceedings are taken` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(8) Attorney General` TRUE `s 810.01(8) the lawful deputy of one of them` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(8) Attorney General` TRUE `s 810.01(8) another person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.01(8) Attorney General` FALSE `s 810.01(8) the Attorney General of Canada` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 810.011`

#ASSERT `s 810.011(1) the person may lay an information before a provincial court judge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(1) the person may lay an information before a provincial court judge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(2) the provincial court judge may cause the parties to appear` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(2) the provincial court judge may cause the parties to appear` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(3) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(3) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance, with or without sureties` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(3) the period of the recognizance is not more than 12 months` 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(3) the period of the recognizance is not more than 12 months` 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(4) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a longer period` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(4) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a longer period` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(4) the longer period of the recognizance is not more than five years` 60 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(4) the longer period of the recognizance is not more than five years` 61 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(5) the provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(5) the provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(5) the term of imprisonment is not more than 12 months` 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(5) the term of imprisonment is not more than 12 months` 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(6) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.011(6)(a) to participate in a treatment program` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(6) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.011(6)(b) to wear an electronic monitoring device` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(6) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.011(6)(b) to wear an electronic monitoring device` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(6) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.011(6)(c) to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(6) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.011(6)(d) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(6) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.011(6)(e) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(6) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.011(6)(f) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(6) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` `s 810.011(6) another reasonable condition` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(7) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(7) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(7) the provincial court judge is required to add the firearms condition and specify the period during which it applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(7) the provincial court judge is required to add the firearms condition and specify the period during which it applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(8) the provincial court judge is required to specify in the recognizance how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(8) the provincial court judge is required to specify in the recognizance how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(9) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a passport condition is desirable` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(9) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a passport condition is desirable` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(9) the provincial court judge is required to add the passport condition and specify the period during which it applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(9) the provincial court judge is required to add the passport condition and specify the period during which it applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(10) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a geographic-area condition is desirable` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(10) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a geographic-area condition is desirable` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(10) the provincial court judge is required to add the geographic-area condition and specify the period during which it applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(10) the provincial court judge is required to add the geographic-area condition and specify the period during which it applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(11) the provincial court judge is required to include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(11) the provincial court judge is required to include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(12) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(12) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(12) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(12) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(13) subsections 810(4) and (5) apply to the recognizance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(13) subsections 810(4) and (5) apply to the recognizance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.011(14) Attorney General` TRUE `s 810.011(14) the Attorney General of Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(14) Attorney General` TRUE `s 810.011(14) the Attorney General of the province in which the proceedings are taken` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(14) Attorney General` TRUE `s 810.011(14) the lawful deputy of one of them` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(14) Attorney General` TRUE `s 810.011(14) another person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.011(14) Attorney General` FALSE `s 810.011(14) the Attorney General of Canada` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulative rules -- sections 810, 810.01 and 810.011`

-- Run with #TRACE and read: each duty is fulfilled when the named party does the action.
#TRACE `s 810(2) the justice is to cause the parties to appear` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a justice` DOES `s 810(2) cause the parties to appear` AT 1
#TRACE `s 810(3.1) the justice or court is to consider the firearms condition` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a justice` DOES `s 810(3.1) consider the firearms condition` AT 1
    PARTY `a justice` DOES `s 810(3.1) add the firearms condition` AT 2
#TRACE `s 810(3.11) the justice or court is to specify the manner and method` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a justice` DOES `s 810(3.11) specify the manner of surrender` AT 1
#TRACE `s 810(3.12) the justice or court is to include a statement of reasons in the record` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a justice` DOES `s 810(3.12) include a statement of reasons in the record` AT 1
#TRACE `s 810(3.2) the justice or court is to consider the supplementary conditions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a justice` DOES `s 810(3.2) consider the supplementary conditions` AT 1
#TRACE `s 810.01(5) the judge is to consider the firearms condition` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a provincial court judge` DOES `s 810.01(5) consider the firearms condition` AT 1
    PARTY `a provincial court judge` DOES `s 810.01(5) add the firearms condition and specify the period` AT 2
#TRACE `s 810.01(5.1) the judge is to specify how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a provincial court judge` DOES `s 810.01(5.1) specify how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered` AT 1
#TRACE `s 810.01(5.2) the judge is to include a statement of reasons in the record` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a provincial court judge` DOES `s 810.01(5.2) include a statement of reasons in the record` AT 1
#TRACE `s 810.011(15) the Attorney General of Canada is to prepare and lay the annual report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Attorney General of Canada` DOES `s 810.011(15) prepare the annual report and cause it to be laid before each House of Parliament` AT 1
